+/// Performs the same sequence as [`accept_udp`], bounded by the same
+/// `config.accept_timeout`, but reads and writes through `io` instead of a
+/// socket of its own. MS-RDPEUDP 2.1 and 3.1.3 have the server take every
+/// connection on one UDP port, which a socket per connection cannot do: a
+/// server that listens that way demultiplexes the port by peer and passes
+/// each peer's datagrams here.
+///
+/// `io` must report its peer ([`DatagramIo::peer_addr`]), and its first
